=== vocabulary ===
A ledger is a kind of storage.
A batch is a kind of process.
A record is a kind of thing.
A constraint is a kind of thing.
An audit row is a kind of thing.
An index job is a kind of process.
A trigger phrase is a kind of thing.

A ledger has a name, a status, and an updated at.
A batch has a name, a status, a ledger id, and an updated at.
A record has a key, a status, a checksum, and an updated at.
A constraint has a name, a status, and a table name.
An audit row has a key, a status, a table name, and an updated at.
An index job has a name, a status, and an updated at.
A trigger phrase has a text.

Definition: a ledger is open if its status is "open".
Definition: a batch is ready if its status is "ready".
Definition: a batch is settled if its status is "settled".
Definition: a record is stale if its updated at is within the last 30 days.
Definition: a record is duplicate if its status is "duplicate".
Definition: a constraint is violated if its status is "violated".
Definition: an audit row is orphaned if its status is "orphaned".
Definition: an index job is lagging if its updated at is within the last 7 days.

Settlement relates a batch to a ledger.
Settlement is read via the batch.settle tool.
Canonicalization relates a record to an audit row.
Canonicalization is read via the record.mark_canonical tool.
Auditing relates a ledger to an audit row.
Auditing is read via the audit_row.list tool.

The verb to settle (it settles, it is settled) means the settlement relation.
The verb to canonicalize (it canonicalizes, it is canonicalized) means the canonicalization relation.
The verb to audit (it audits, it is audited) means the auditing relation.

To fetch ready batches:
  bind batches = invoke batch.list with status = "ready".

To fetch stale records:
  bind records = invoke record.list with status = "stale".

To fetch duplicate records:
  bind records = invoke record.list with status = "duplicate".

To fetch violated constraints:
  bind constraints = invoke constraint.list with status = "violated".

To fetch orphaned audit rows:
  bind audit rows = invoke audit_row.list with status = "orphaned".

To fetch lagging index jobs:
  bind index jobs = invoke index.list with status = "lagging".

To reconcile a ledger:
  bind result = invoke ledger.reconcile with ledger = the ledger.

To settle a batch:
  bind settlement = invoke batch.settle with batch = the batch.

To mark a record canonical:
  invoke record.mark_canonical with record = the record.

To rebuild an index job:
  bind job = invoke index.rebuild with index job = the index job.

To purge a record:
  invoke record.purge with record = the record.

=== tools ===
List Batches
============
-- List batches by status.
~ batch.list(status: String) : List

List Records
============
-- List records by status.
~ record.list(status: String) : List

List Constraints
================
-- List constraints by status.
~ constraint.list(status: String) : List

List Audit Rows
===============
-- List audit rows by status.
~ audit_row.list(status: String) : List

List Index Jobs
===============
-- List index jobs by status.
~ index.list(status: String) : List

Reconcile Ledger
================
-- Reconcile a ledger.
~ ledger.reconcile(ledger: Ledger) : Boolean

Settle Batch
============
-- Settle a batch.
~ batch.settle(batch: Batch) : Boolean

Mark Canonical
==============
-- Mark a record canonical.
~ record.mark_canonical(record: Record) : Boolean

Rebuild Index
=============
-- Rebuild an index.
~ index.rebuild(indexJob: IndexJob) : IndexJob

Purge Record
============
-- Purge a record.
~ record.purge(record: Record) : Boolean
